<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal farm output to fall due to lack of rain.</title>
<headline>Portugal farm output to fall due to lack of rain.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A lack of rainfall in the first two weeks of April will contribute to a reduction in agricultural production in Portugal this year, compared with 1996, the state-run National Statistics Institute (INE) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The lack of rain delayed the spring sowing and hindered the normal germination of crops,&quot; INE said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;For these crops, our forecasts point to a reduction in cultivated areas, compared with the previous year.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;In the first two weeks of April, the weather remained hot and dry, prolonging the drought conditions that have been recorded since the beginning of the year,&quot; it said.</p>
